  "description": "Reid Tract Jr. 26 | 26\" Kids' mountain bike\nBuilt for young adventurers aged 10–13, the Reid Tract Jr. 26 is a kids' mountain bike designed for everything from neighbourhood rides to off-road adventures. With a tough yet lightweight 6061 alloy frame, front suspension, wide tyres and powerful cable disc brakes, it's built to give young riders confidence across a variety of terrain.\nThe alloy frame features increased step-over clearance for easier mounting and dismounting, while aluminium kids' specific components help keep the bike lightweight and easy to handle.\nThe 50mm front suspension helps keep bumps at bay, while double-wall alloy rims and wide 2.35\" tyres provide grip and stability on the trail. Shimano 7-speed Tourney gearing gives young riders a useful range for tackling changing terrain, while powerful cable disc brakes provide reliable stopping power and control.\nWhether they're riding around the neighbourhood, exploring local trails or heading out with family and friends, the Tract Jr. 26 is built to help young riders keep up with their parents and peers while enjoying the freedom of riding outdoors.\nWho is the Tract Jr. 26 for?\nThe Tract Jr. 26\" Kids' Mountain Bike is ideal for:\n\nYoung riders aged 10–13\nKids who want to explore neighbourhoods, parks and trails\nRiders looking for a tough but lightweight alloy mountain bike\nYoung cyclists who want 7-speed gearing\nRiders who want front suspension and wide tyres for varied terrain\nKids who want to ride alongside parents and peers\nFamily rides, outdoor adventures and weekend trail trips\n\nFind the right fit\nThe Tract Jr. 26 features 26\" wheels and is designed for riders aged 10–13. Use our Kids' Bike Size Guide by clicking the tab above to find the right bike based on your child's height and age.",
